
**Added after review:** GitSync now refuses content only when the check found it at fault. `conf_rehash_abandoned()` says why the rehash was abandoned: `CONF_ABANDON_ERRORS` when the check found errors in the file or crashed on it, `CONF_ABANDON_OTHER` when the file could not be read or kept changing while it was checked. On the second, nothing is known of the content, so GitSync puts its file back, says so, and tries the content again at the next sync. Before, it ran the quiet check, found the restored configuration clean, and refused content that had never been checked until the next commit. The full CMocka suite passes. I did not reproduce the kept-changing case live, since it needs a writer racing the check.
